ax342547.SymmetricFactorization:0"],"kind":"concept","label":"Symmetric low-rank factorization, including characteristic two","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.SymmetricFactorization","semanticId":"Lax342547.SymmetricFactorization","tooltipHtml":"Symmetric low-rank factorization, including characteristic two"},"c:Lax342547.UnaryMixer":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547.UnaryMixer.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryMixer:0"],"kind":"concept","label":"Formal forward and reverse rows of a unary mixer test","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.UnaryMixer","semanticId":"Lax342547.UnaryMixer","tooltipHtml":"Formal forward and reverse rows of a unary mixer test"},"c:Lax342547.UnaryRowLaw":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547.UnaryRowLaw.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryRowLaw:0"],"kind":"concept","label":"Joint distribution of the unary mixer row matrix","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.UnaryRowLaw","semanticId":"Lax342547.UnaryRowLaw","tooltipHtml":"Joint distribution of the unary mixer row matrix"},"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n:conclusion:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Use the explicit threshold, independent of n and of the tester family.\nThe finite union bound then yields mixers satisfying every unary test\nfor each n above that threshold, before any unit law is introduced.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n","tooltipHtml":"Use the explicit threshold, independent of n and of the tester family.\nThe finite union bound then yields mixers satisfying every unary test\nfor each n above that threshold, before any unit law is introduced."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one:conclusion:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"If every mixer choice failed, the bad event would be the whole finite\nprobability space and would have mass one. The explicit union bound\nbelow one therefore leaves a simultaneous successful choice.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_of_failureBound_lt_one","tooltipHtml":"If every mixer choice failed, the bad event would be the whole finite\nprobability space and would have mass one. The explicit union bound\nbelow one therefore leaves a simultaneous successful choice."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.exists_for_large_n:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary:conclusion:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Choose simultaneous successful unary mixers above the explicit\nthreshold. For each profile, tag, and label, use its factorization to\ndefine the bounded row space before any non-Z values are specified.\nThe row-space dependence and polar-rank bound then hold for every\nallowed fixing with that same space.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.exists_uniform_unary","tooltipHtml":"Choose simultaneous successful unary mixers above the explicit\nthreshold. For each profile, tag, and label, use its factorization to\ndefine the bounded row space before any non-Z values are specified.\nThe row-space dependence and polar-rank bound then hold for every\nallowed fixing with that same space."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_le_geometric":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_le_geometric.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_le_geometric:assumption:Lax342547.CoordinateCounts:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_le_geometric:conclusion:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.failureBound_le_geometric:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Separate the profile-count exponent into its constant part and its slope\nin n. The unary corank exponent exceeds that slope by at least one,\nleaving the explicit constant threshold times 2^(-n).","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_le_geometric","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_le_geometric","tooltipHtml":"Separate the profile-count exponent into its constant part and its slope\nin n. The unary corank exponent exceeds that slope by at least one,\nleaving the explicit constant threshold times 2^(-n)."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one:assumption:Lax342547.CoordinateCounts:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one:conclusion:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Substitute the proved coordinate count. The numerator is C times\n2^(a n), with C independent of n and a the displayed profile-count\nslope. The denominator exponent is at least (a+1)n. For n≥C, the\nelementary inequality n<2^n makes the resulting bound strictly below one.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.failureBound_lt_one","tooltipHtml":"Substitute the proved coordinate count. The numerator is C times\n2^(a n), with C independent of n and a the displayed profile-count\nslope. The denominator exponent is at least (a+1)n. For n≥C, the\nelementary inequality n&lt;2^n makes the resulting bound strictly below one."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound:assumption:Lax342547.ProfileCounting:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryRowLaw:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound:conclusion:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Take the finite union over the actual low-rank profile space, tags,\nand labels. The profile-count bound controls the number of tests, and\neach event already includes every fixing of the non-Z coordinates.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.simultaneous_failure_bound","tooltipHtml":"Take the finite union over the actual low-rank profile space, tags,\nand labels. The profile-count bound controls the number of tests, and\neach event already includes every fixing of the non-Z coordinates."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good:assumption:Lax342547.SymmetricFactorization:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good:assumption:Lax342547.UnaryMixer:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good:conclusion:Lax342547.UnaryMixers.uniform_of_good:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"For each profile, tag, and label, its symmetric component factorization\ndetermines a bounded row space before 